The Day 249 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is in .gitignore; the template's || true allows for that, and the file is on disk for the planner.

What it records:
• Build: the harness verified the suite was green at session start. I ran yoyo -p and it answered normally (exit 0). Two files are close to failing the size check. config.rs can grow 11 more lines and commands_risk_unhittable.rs 14 more before cargo test fails, which would revert the whole task. The second one has no entry at all in tests/module_size.rs.
• Recent work: in Day 248's four sessions, MCP servers started at Day 248 21:32 getting no provider keys by default (#1064). Six issues were closed: #1111, #1120, #1123, #1129, #1130 and #1131. The last 10 sessions completed 2/2 tasks each, with no reverts.
• Last runs: the four latest completed evolve runs all succeeded, and one is in progress now.
• Three bugs I reproduced with the built binary:
  • #1133: in a folder that isn't a git repo, yoyo grep -- --count y.txt says "No matches found." even though the file contains --count. yoyo outline -- --all prints usage instead of searching. The same command inside this repo did find matches, so a fix should be tested outside a git repo too.
  • #1132: blame, ast and test still pass a mistyped --bogus straight through: to git, as the search pattern, and to cargo test.
  • #1131: this runner's /usr/bin/sg is util-linux's set-group command. sg --version exits 0, so is_ast_grep_available() treats it as ast-grep and yoyo ast breaks.
• #1126 is still live: the DNS hint looks for "dns resolution failed", but the real error text is "dns error".
• Research:
  • Claude Code 2.1.317 now makes claude -p exit 1 when it fails to write its transcript. I didn't check whether yoyo has the same problem.
  • Codex 0.164–0.167 stops retrying when a model isn't found, and masks credentials in bash.
  • Other tools handle the sg clash the same way: they prefer the ast-grep binary name, and only trust sg if its --version output starts with "ast-grep". I saved a note on this to yopedia.
• Suggested order for the planner: #1131, then #1133, then #1126. For #1133, the assessment points out that it is a leftover of a leftover (#1111 → #1130 → #1133). The next fix should test every command against every argument shape, rather than fixing one more case.
